                <pb facs="0165" n="45" sameAs="frus:frus1905/pg45"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to Minister Beaupré.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1905-09-14"><hi rendition="#italic">September 14,
                        1905</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Loomis informs Mr. Beaupré that, according to telegraphic advices from
                    leading manufacturers of agricultural implements, the Argentine Government
                    proposes to impose a prohibitory tariff upon all repair parts of agricultural
                    machinery, and as the imposition of such tariff will inflict great loss upon an
                    important American industry and will work great harm instructs him to represent
                    to the Argentine Government the injustice of applying a higher rate of duty to
                    the necessary integral parts of the machine than to the machine itself and to
                    keep the Department informed.)</p>
            </div>
